---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<Base title="Vendor Onboarding for MSPs | HeyDock" description="How IT providers start white-label work with HeyDock, including contacts, paperwork and a first work order. Document packs are discussed privately." canonicalPath="/vendor-onboarding">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Vendor onboarding</p>
    <h1>MSP onboarding without surprises</h1>
    <p class="lede">How IT providers start white-label work with HeyDock. Document packs and insurance evidence are discussed privately when needed—they are not automatically published here.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section white"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Typical steps</h2>
    <ol class="process" style="margin:1.5rem 0 2.5rem">
      <li><span class="num">1</span><h3>Intro and fit</h3><p>Confirm services, geographies of interest and commercial model.</p></li>
      <li><span class="num">2</span><h3>Contacts</h3><p>Exchange escalation owners, branding rules and reporting format.</p></li>
      <li><span class="num">3</span><h3>Paperwork</h3><p>Discuss NDA, MSA, SOW, SLA, DPA or insurance evidence when applicable.</p></li>
      <li><span class="num">4</span><h3>First work order</h3><p>Pilot a clearly scoped visit or project before wider volume.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Communication and control</h2>
      <p>Partners keep the customer relationship unless a work order says otherwise. HeyDock follows partner branding and communication rules agreed in writing. Scope changes require partner approval. Reporting and escalation paths are named per work order.</p>
      <h2>What can be discussed</h2>
      <p>An NDA, master services agreement, statement of work, service levels, data-processing terms or insurance evidence can be discussed or shared privately when applicable to a partnership. This website does not imply that any specific document or insurance certificate already exists or is available for public download unless a verified file is linked from <a href="/documents">Documents and policies</a>.</p>
      <p>See also the <a href="/partners">IT partners overview</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <CtaBand title="Discuss white-label support" />
</Base>
